# ── HTS testing: the PBIX's TWO project sections ───────────────────
# Every testing visual in the report is bound to the measure `HTS Tested`,
# whose DAX reads:
#     VAR _OurProjectElements   = { 17 Jamii / Daraja elements }   (JTP)
#     VAR _OtherProjectElements = { 28 CHAP Stawisha elements }
#     VAR _CombinedElements     = UNION(_OurProjectElements, _OtherProjectElements)
#     RETURN CALCULATE(SUM('Data Element Values'[Value]),
#                      'Data Elements'[Data Element] IN _CombinedElements)
# i.e. it ADDS BOTH projects.  Verified by reading the report layout itself
# (Report/definition/pages/**/visual.json): `HTS Tested` is on "Total tested
# for HIV Monthly Performance" (lineChart), "TESTING TREND BY COUNTY",
# "Total tested by Sex" / "by Age" and the HTS performance cards.  No visual
# in the report references the our-project-only measure `HTS Tested 1`.
#
# The two namespaces are also disjoint at facility level, so the union cannot
# double count: for 202606 the entire 7,187 of the 28-element total sits on
# the 62 CHAP Stawisha facilities and exactly 0 on the other 197.
HTS_TESTED_OUR = list(_HTS_TST_JAMII_17)              # 17 x JTP (Jamii/Daraja)
HTS_TESTED_OTHER = list(_STA_HTS_TESTED)              # 28 x CHAP Stawisha
HTS_TESTED_ALL = HTS_TESTED_OUR + HTS_TESTED_OTHER    # 45 = PBIX `HTS Tested`

# The same two sections for positives.  The PBIX measure is
# `HTS_Testing_Positives` = the SAME element list as `HTS_Testing_General`
# wrapped in `KEEPFILTERS('HIV Results'[HIV Results] == "HIV+")`, so the JTP
# half is the 15 `HTS_TST (facility) - *` elements CUT TO THEIR HIV+ CATEGORY
# OPTION COMBOS, plus the SNS "(Pos) - Tested peers" element (its name already
# means positive, so it must NOT be COC-filtered).  The Stawisha half is the
# 28 "... New Positive" elements, which also bake positivity into the name.
#
# 🔥 `smzxVpKXbR5` ("HTS_TST_POS : Numerator") is NOT this measure.  It is a
# standalone DHIS2 *indicator* whose numerator does not equal the 15 facility
# elements @ HIV+ (221 vs 245 for all counties @202606), so using it made the
# HIV Testing page show 366 positives where the PBIX shows 390 — a 24-record
# under-report, and a different number from `/pbix/api/hts-summary` for the
# very same metric.  Same defect `pbix_dashboards._hts_positive_periods`
# already documents and avoids.
HTS_POSITIVE_OUR15 = list(_HTS_TST_JAMII_17[:15])     # 15 x HTS_TST (facility)
# SNS "(Pos) - Tested peers" ONLY — the HRN twin counts *tested* peers, not
# positives, and the 15 facility elements above exclude both by construction.
# Matches `pbix_dashboards.HTS_POSITIVE_SNS`.
HTS_POSITIVE_SNS = ["FITo7mucBoA"]
HTS_POSITIVE_OUR = HTS_POSITIVE_OUR15                 # needs HTS_POSITIVE_COCS
HTS_POSITIVE_OTHER = list(_STA_HTS_POSITIVE)          # 28 x CHAP Stawisha
HTS_POSITIVE_ALL = (HTS_POSITIVE_OUR + HTS_POSITIVE_SNS
                    + HTS_POSITIVE_OTHER)             # 44 = PBIX `HTS Positive`

